WEBVTT

00:08.975 --> 00:10.472
Hey.

00:15.575 --> 00:17.906
This is no place to be right now.

00:21.375 --> 00:22.973
So fly away.

00:24.908 --> 00:28.424
You've got wings. Use them.

00:28.508 --> 00:29.424
Falco!

00:29.508 --> 00:31.624
Brother? Why are you here?

00:31.708 --> 00:33.424
Good. I'm glad you're
able to talk at least.

00:33.508 --> 00:34.772
Colt, move!

00:35.708 --> 00:38.372
I'll carry you back.
Try to hold on!

00:48.708 --> 00:49.772
Falco!

00:56.108 --> 00:58.505
Report. What happened, Colt?

01:00.708 --> 01:03.624
The Eldian advance squad
has been wiped out.

01:03.708 --> 01:07.291
They took a direct hit
from an artillery shell

01:07.375 --> 01:09.824
and got blown to bits.

01:09.908 --> 01:11.624
What of the trench?

01:11.708 --> 01:14.624
It's hopeless.
We can't dig any further!

01:14.708 --> 01:16.958
Oh? And who decided that?

01:17.042 --> 01:18.958
Are you trying to give
me orders now, Eldian?

01:19.042 --> 01:20.691
Insubordinate mutt!

01:20.775 --> 01:22.558
You watch your tone
with Commander Magath!

01:22.642 --> 01:26.024
But, sir. If things
keep going like this...

01:26.108 --> 01:28.424
Falco. You look like
you're drunk.

01:28.508 --> 01:30.624
Guess he must've hit
his head pretty good.

01:30.708 --> 01:33.024
How much of the last four years
do you remember, Falco?

01:33.108 --> 01:34.824
You know we're at war, right?

01:34.908 --> 01:36.558
Who are you people?

01:36.642 --> 01:38.024
Where am I?

01:38.108 --> 01:40.357
I don't get it.

01:40.441 --> 01:44.624
Wasn't I just flying around with
a couple of swords in my hands?

01:44.708 --> 01:49.024
Whoo. Like that.
And there were Titans, too...

01:49.108 --> 01:50.958
Okay. It sounds like
we're gonna have to

01:51.042 --> 01:53.424
re-explain the entire operation.

01:53.508 --> 01:55.424
Just do your best to keep up, Falco.

01:55.508 --> 01:56.424
Here goes:

01:56.508 --> 01:59.024
This war's dragged on for four years now,

01:59.108 --> 02:01.639
but with this battle, we can end it.

02:02.508 --> 02:05.424
All we have to do is capture Fort Slava.

02:05.508 --> 02:07.357
Well, to be exact, we have to destroy

02:07.441 --> 02:11.491
the Mid-East Allied Forces'
fleet in the harbor beneath it.

02:11.575 --> 02:13.291
Once those ships are sunk,

02:13.375 --> 02:15.624
we'll have won this war for Marley.

02:15.708 --> 02:19.024
But Fort Slava defends the high
ground overlooking the harbor,

02:19.107 --> 02:21.357
which means there's
no attacking that fleet

02:21.441 --> 02:24.824
from land without control of the fort.

02:24.908 --> 02:26.824
So why can't the Marleyan fleet just

02:26.908 --> 02:27.824
attack them from the sea?

02:27.908 --> 02:28.958
Come on, Zofia!

02:29.042 --> 02:31.558
Do you really think we can count
on that navy to do a thing?

02:31.642 --> 02:33.357
It took them four
whole years to establish

02:33.441 --> 02:35.624
any vestige of control over the seas!

02:35.708 --> 02:37.424
And this shouldn't really be a surprise,

02:37.508 --> 02:40.291
but they lost half their damn
battleships in the process!

02:40.375 --> 02:42.024
So of course they're
too chickenshit to do

02:42.107 --> 02:43.758
a single friggin' thing
until we've taken this

02:43.842 --> 02:46.291
massive death trap of a fort for them!

02:46.375 --> 02:48.424
Screw every single one of those
stupid, incompetent cowards!

02:48.508 --> 02:52.024
Udo. Calm it down before
you squeeze Falco's head off.

02:52.107 --> 02:54.758
Oh, uh. Sorry.

02:54.842 --> 02:56.024
So what gives?

02:56.107 --> 02:57.958
Why did they send us to the front lines?

02:58.042 --> 02:59.491
It's not like four warrior candidates

02:59.575 --> 03:01.024
can make a real difference.

03:01.107 --> 03:03.424
First of all, you can speak for yourself.

03:03.508 --> 03:05.624
Second, they wanna judge us.

03:05.708 --> 03:07.939
They're choosing their next warrior.

03:09.708 --> 03:11.558
The time is almost here.

03:11.642 --> 03:13.691
Commander Magath chose the front lines

03:13.775 --> 03:15.958
for the location of our final test.

03:16.041 --> 03:18.439
He knows what's on the horizon.

03:19.175 --> 03:21.357
The person he chooses
will be at the center

03:21.441 --> 03:23.758
of the plan to conquer Paradis.

03:23.842 --> 03:26.506
The successor to the Armored Titan.

05:07.642 --> 05:09.572
The Armored Titan.

05:10.508 --> 05:13.639
I wonder which one of us it'll be.

05:15.842 --> 05:17.624
Shut up. No you don't.

05:17.708 --> 05:19.491
You've made it perfectly
clear that you don't think

05:19.575 --> 05:21.558
any of us come close to you, Gabi.

05:21.642 --> 05:24.358
Well yeah, that's because you don't.

05:24.442 --> 05:27.358
True. Gabi has us
three soundly beat.

05:27.442 --> 05:29.624
Tch. Not in terms
of grades, she doesn't.

05:29.708 --> 05:32.558
No. They don't care
about our grades, Udo.

05:32.642 --> 05:34.358
It's like I keep telling you.

05:34.442 --> 05:36.358
The difference between
me and the three of you

05:36.442 --> 05:37.957
is that I'm prepared.

05:38.041 --> 05:40.824
To shoulder the fate of us Eldians,

05:40.907 --> 05:44.624
and purge that island of devils
who've only made us suffer.

05:44.708 --> 05:46.824
I'll slaughter every one of them.

05:46.907 --> 05:48.758
I'll win that war, and prove to the world

05:48.842 --> 05:51.024
they don't have to fear us anymore.

05:51.108 --> 05:53.957
That the only Eldians
left are good Eldians!

05:54.516 --> 05:56.233
I won't be defeated.

05:56.317 --> 05:59.814
Not until everyone in the
internment zone is set free.

06:02.382 --> 06:05.347
Hey. Just what are
you doing with those?

06:06.516 --> 06:08.499
Looks cool. Right?

06:08.583 --> 06:10.432
It won't work, Commander Magath!

06:10.516 --> 06:12.233
If we try to take out the railway tracks

06:12.317 --> 06:14.499
with nothing but infantry,
we'll get mowed down

06:14.583 --> 06:17.033
by machine-gun fire
before we can do a thing.

06:17.117 --> 06:20.833
That trench is fully manned.
It's an airtight defense.

06:20.917 --> 06:22.233
On top of that, they have artillery

06:22.317 --> 06:24.499
supporting them from inside the fort.

06:24.583 --> 06:26.899
If we stay put,
it's only a matter of time

06:26.983 --> 06:29.833
before shells start
raining down on our heads.

06:29.917 --> 06:33.299
It sounds like you
have an idea. Go on.

06:33.382 --> 06:34.432
Let's use them.

06:34.516 --> 06:37.300
We need to unleash Jaws and Cart now.

06:37.383 --> 06:39.499
Galliard and Pieck
should be able to do it.

06:39.583 --> 06:41.299
They can wipe out
the enemies in the trench

06:41.382 --> 06:43.432
and the pillbox in the blink of an eye.

06:43.516 --> 06:44.348
Won't work.

06:45.583 --> 06:48.499
They'll beat us if we're playing
our cards the wrong way.

06:48.583 --> 06:51.081
Commander Magath.
It's coming through now.

06:52.117 --> 06:53.814
What is, sir?

06:54.917 --> 06:58.033
A train. An armored train.

06:58.117 --> 07:00.033
Equipped with two big guns in the front,

07:00.117 --> 07:01.833
and two more in the back.

07:01.917 --> 07:04.099
They're the Allied Forces'
newest weapons:

07:04.183 --> 07:06.033
Anti-Titan cannons.

07:06.117 --> 07:09.499
They fire 150-millimeter
armor piercing shells,

07:09.583 --> 07:13.033
capable of bringing down
a Titan with a single shot.

07:13.117 --> 07:14.233
Even one of the Nine.

07:14.316 --> 07:18.298
Maybe, but both of our Titans
are incredibly fast, sir.

07:18.382 --> 07:19.967
The odds of them getting
hit in the neck are so...

07:20.051 --> 07:22.298
And, what if it happens?

07:22.382 --> 07:26.099
We'd lose a warrior, and the
power of yet another Titan.

07:26.183 --> 07:27.298
Plus there's no guarantee

07:27.382 --> 07:29.499
that we'd be able to reclaim that power.

07:29.583 --> 07:32.499
That's right. We'd be
repeating the mistake we made

07:32.583 --> 07:35.499
when we tried to take the
Founding Titan nine years ago.

07:35.583 --> 07:37.099
We're two Titans down.

07:37.183 --> 07:39.833
We need to protect the ones we have left.

07:39.917 --> 07:42.033
The loss of the Colossal
and Female Titans

07:42.117 --> 07:44.899
caused a perceived lapse
in Marley's strength.

07:44.983 --> 07:49.298
That sparked this war and
delayed the Paradis Operation.

07:49.382 --> 07:50.899
What is it that makes our motherland

07:50.983 --> 07:53.232
the great empire it is today?

07:53.316 --> 07:55.432
The Nine, sir. Or the seven.

07:55.516 --> 07:56.633
Five now.

07:56.717 --> 08:00.033
And our nation won't last if
we keep throwing them away.

08:00.117 --> 08:02.432
The power of Marley's Titans is absolute,

08:02.516 --> 08:05.432
that is a fact which must never change.

08:05.516 --> 08:08.299
Line up the Eldians.
Have them prepare for a charge.

08:08.383 --> 08:09.099
Yes, sir!

08:09.183 --> 08:11.033
Please reconsider!
If they charge...

08:11.117 --> 08:12.899
What's the matter, Eldian?

08:12.983 --> 08:15.033
Are you not loyal soldiers who've sworn

08:15.117 --> 08:17.280
to fight and die for Marley?

08:19.583 --> 08:23.033
This is a chance for the 800 Eldians here

08:23.117 --> 08:26.948
to atone for the past and serve
our motherland with honor.

08:32.383 --> 08:34.833
Yes. All creatures drink
of joy at nature's breast.

08:34.917 --> 08:36.432
All Right.
Soldiers at the ready!

08:36.516 --> 08:38.681
Up! Prepare to attack!

08:39.917 --> 08:42.232
Come on! Stand up!

08:42.316 --> 08:46.033
Eldians! Your target is
the enemy railway track.

08:46.117 --> 08:49.432
It's well defended, but you
must succeed at any cost.

08:49.516 --> 08:50.699
Guard the suicide squad.

08:50.783 --> 08:54.833
They'll charge the enemy bunker
and disable their machine gun.

08:54.917 --> 08:57.766
You may be spawn of the devil,
but through your actions here,

08:57.850 --> 09:00.099
you can cleanse yourselves
of that disgrace!

09:00.182 --> 09:03.099
This is your chance to honor
and be honored in turn

09:03.182 --> 09:05.166
by our motherland!

09:05.250 --> 09:06.899
Prepare to prove your worth.

09:06.983 --> 09:08.499
Yes, sir!

09:08.583 --> 09:11.432
You Warrior candidates
will stand by here.

09:11.516 --> 09:13.833
If I have to trade 800 Eldian soldiers

09:13.917 --> 09:15.899
to take out those tracks, then so be it,

09:15.983 --> 09:18.499
but the tracks must be destroyed.

09:18.583 --> 09:22.366
As long as that armored train is
prowling the fort's perimeter,

09:22.450 --> 09:25.033
neither Beast nor Armored
can be called upon

09:25.117 --> 09:26.299
to finish the job.

09:26.383 --> 09:27.948
Yeah. I know, but...

09:29.182 --> 09:30.033
Look, Colt.

09:30.117 --> 09:32.433
You're the chosen successor
of the Beast Titan.

09:32.517 --> 09:34.366
You need to take a page from Zeke's book

09:34.450 --> 09:36.380
and learn what it means to lead.

09:44.183 --> 09:47.899
Perfect. We can destroy
the tracks and the train.

09:47.983 --> 09:50.299
Why don't'cha let me handle this, sir?

09:50.383 --> 09:51.099
Huh?

09:51.182 --> 09:53.833
Ta-da! If you'll let me.

09:53.917 --> 09:57.048
I'm sure that I can take out
that armored train by myself!

09:58.850 --> 10:00.299
Hey. Wait.

10:00.383 --> 10:02.299
You're too valuable an asset.

10:02.383 --> 10:06.033
This country spent a lot of
money to train you. Denied.

10:06.116 --> 10:08.033
It's true. I'm super valuable,

10:08.116 --> 10:10.299
especially compared to these three.

10:10.383 --> 10:13.098
Honestly, you might never
find a warrior candidate

10:13.182 --> 10:15.299
who's as talented as me.

10:15.383 --> 10:18.499
Even then. They won't
be this cute.

10:18.583 --> 10:20.833
But if I pull this off,
you can take out the train

10:20.917 --> 10:24.299
without needing to sacrifice
that 800-man unit!

10:24.383 --> 10:25.899
And if you fail?

10:25.983 --> 10:28.899
Then you'll lose your
most promising candidate,

10:28.983 --> 10:31.681
as well as a bundle of
seven hand grenades.

10:35.051 --> 10:37.899
That said, sir, if you really
think I'm more valuable

10:37.983 --> 10:41.099
than 800 Eldian infantrymen, I get it.

10:41.183 --> 10:44.232
To think that you'd sacrifice
that many soldiers just for me.

10:44.316 --> 10:47.098
I knew you loved me deep down,
but I didn't know how deep.

10:47.182 --> 10:50.899
Fine. Go ahead.

10:50.983 --> 10:51.899
No. Gabi.

10:51.983 --> 10:53.033
Mark my words.

10:53.116 --> 10:56.098
I'll destroy that train and
prove no warrior candidate

10:56.182 --> 10:58.881
deserves to inherit
the Armor more than me.

11:02.583 --> 11:04.499
What are you doing?

11:04.583 --> 11:07.967
My plan won't work
if I'm in uniform, sir.

11:08.050 --> 11:11.098
With your permission, I'd like
to remove my armband as well.

11:11.182 --> 11:12.180
Granted.

11:19.183 --> 11:22.214
Hey. There's someone
coming. Look there.

11:24.450 --> 11:27.299
It's a woman. A girl, really.

11:27.383 --> 11:29.099
Looks like she's trying to surrender.

11:29.183 --> 11:32.099
Yeah, right. Don't trust it,
she could be Eldian.

11:32.183 --> 11:35.366
She's limping, as if she's
wounded or something.

11:35.450 --> 11:37.848
Maybe her foot's been shackled?

11:38.983 --> 11:41.232
Who
cares? She probably is Eldian.

11:41.316 --> 11:43.099
Shoot her before she transforms!

11:43.183 --> 11:44.499
I don't shoot kids.

11:44.583 --> 11:46.899
You've got a gun:
If you wanna shoot her, do it.

11:46.983 --> 11:49.748
Shit.

11:54.983 --> 11:56.180
What the...?

12:07.583 --> 12:09.114
Not yet.

12:11.851 --> 12:13.147
Wait for it.

12:16.383 --> 12:17.499
Not yet.

12:17.583 --> 12:18.899
She's just lying there.

12:18.982 --> 12:21.114
Who cares? Shoot her!

12:24.917 --> 12:29.514
Here goes nothing!

12:38.517 --> 12:40.232
She pulled it off.

12:40.316 --> 12:42.047
Galliard! You're up!

12:46.317 --> 12:50.099
Dammit! You cowardly bastards.

12:50.183 --> 12:54.233
This... is exactly why

12:54.317 --> 12:56.947
we should kill every one of you on sight.

12:59.250 --> 13:00.233
Gabi!

13:00.317 --> 13:02.147
Hold on. Falco!

13:20.383 --> 13:22.180
Galliard, thank you!

13:37.583 --> 13:40.299
Our forces have disabled
the armored train.

13:40.383 --> 13:43.299
We can now commence the airborne assault.

13:43.383 --> 13:45.966
The plan from this point
is straightforward.

13:46.050 --> 13:49.781
Zeke will be our spear,
and Reiner our shield.

14:55.670 --> 14:57.518
That really hurts, damn it.

14:57.602 --> 14:58.585
I'm a Marleyan, so why...

14:58.669 --> 14:59.452
'Kay.

14:59.536 --> 15:01.652
Hey, what are you doing? Falco?

15:01.736 --> 15:03.918
Come on. You know.

15:04.002 --> 15:04.652
This guy's done.

15:04.736 --> 15:06.918
He's in no shape to fight anymore.

15:07.002 --> 15:09.385
Udo. Can you spare a tourniquet?

15:09.469 --> 15:12.986
Dumb brat. You should've
just finished him off.

15:13.070 --> 15:16.452
Is this supposed to be your
big selling point, Falco?

15:16.536 --> 15:19.585
You wanna outshine the girl who
just won this battle for Marley

15:19.669 --> 15:22.718
by being a stickler for the laws of war?

15:22.802 --> 15:25.253
This won't help you earn the Armored.

15:25.336 --> 15:26.500
I don't care.

15:27.670 --> 15:29.333
You're such a weirdo.

15:31.402 --> 15:33.399
He's saying something.

15:37.070 --> 15:38.718
Can you interpret?

15:38.802 --> 15:40.252
Tell him that I managed
to stop his bleeding

15:40.336 --> 15:41.385
so he doesn't need to be afra...

15:41.469 --> 15:43.518
"Do not touch me."

15:43.602 --> 15:45.585
"I'll be tainted."

15:45.669 --> 15:48.500
"You filthy devil," he says.

15:59.003 --> 16:00.718
Retreat!

16:00.802 --> 16:02.318
Hurry up!

16:02.402 --> 16:03.518
Get away from the fort!

16:03.602 --> 16:05.667
Don't get caught in it!

16:10.070 --> 16:11.700
It's beginning.

17:35.602 --> 17:37.533
No! Please!

17:44.736 --> 17:48.919
It's true.
You people are devils.

17:49.003 --> 17:51.586
The Marleyans I'm descended from

17:51.670 --> 17:54.252
were preyed upon in the same way.

17:54.336 --> 17:56.852
By Eldians like you.

17:56.936 --> 17:58.400
Fire!

18:08.402 --> 18:10.718
The kinetic bombardment was effective,

18:10.802 --> 18:12.652
but due to the height
they were dropped from,

18:12.736 --> 18:16.919
roughly half the Titans deployed
were killed on impact.

18:17.003 --> 18:20.919
The enemy still has a number
of anti-Titan cannons.

18:21.003 --> 18:23.385
That's 28.29.

18:23.469 --> 18:25.852
I know how many and where they are now.

18:25.936 --> 18:27.433
But still.

18:29.135 --> 18:30.767
Another wall.

18:32.469 --> 18:33.852
I'm sick and tired

18:33.936 --> 18:35.733
of all these walls.

18:54.670 --> 18:55.452
It's the Armored!

18:55.536 --> 18:57.300
Hurry and kill it!

19:04.870 --> 19:06.467
Fire!

19:09.802 --> 19:11.652
The new Anti-Titan shells...

19:11.736 --> 19:13.734
They can even pierce my armor.

19:17.135 --> 19:19.467
What the...? What hit me?

19:21.003 --> 19:23.767
An armored train.
There's another?

19:43.670 --> 19:44.852
Shit!

19:44.936 --> 19:46.200
Fi...

19:51.402 --> 19:52.718
Galliard!

19:52.802 --> 19:54.667
Sons of the devil's whore!

20:27.269 --> 20:28.667
It's done.

20:35.803 --> 20:37.867
So the fort's been cleared.

20:38.602 --> 20:42.734
It's our failure that allowed
this war to happen, Reiner.

20:53.803 --> 20:57.200
But every war is awful, don't you agree?

21:12.002 --> 21:14.719
After four long years,

21:14.803 --> 21:16.567
we're about to win the war.

22:00.536 --> 22:02.652
Following the loss of their fleet,

22:02.736 --> 22:04.985
the Mid-East Allied Forces had no choice

22:05.069 --> 22:08.452
but to sign a peace treaty
on Marley's terms.

22:08.536 --> 22:10.918
It was a long, difficult war for Marley,

22:11.002 --> 22:13.318
but it did end in victory.

22:13.402 --> 22:16.786
However, the war also made it
clear to the whole world

22:16.869 --> 22:19.985
that the power of Titans
would soon be eclipsed.

22:20.069 --> 22:23.719
Knowing this, the leaders of
Marley would resolve to obtain

22:23.803 --> 22:26.734
the Founding Titan
as quickly as possible.

22:27.803 --> 22:29.800
Oh no.

22:33.603 --> 22:36.586
Thanks to the incomparable
bravery of the Marleyan army,

22:36.670 --> 22:38.852
Fort Slava fell and the
Mid-East fleet was sunk!

22:38.936 --> 22:40.918
Yeah! That's incredible!

22:41.002 --> 22:43.599
I knew our soldiers would pull it off!

23:40.536 --> 23:43.052
Titan strength is not absolute.

23:43.136 --> 23:45.719
Marley was shown this painful reality.

23:45.802 --> 23:48.586
Having secured a moment
of peace through their victory,

23:48.670 --> 23:51.719
the Eldians return to
their hometown of Liberio.

23:51.802 --> 23:54.634
Next episode: "Midnight Train."
